@startuml neural-summarizer-pipeline
' Summarizer::extractive end-to-end, including the two short-circuits and the
' index-provenance that the MMR step depends on (and currently breaks — see the note).
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/neural-summarizer-pipeline.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 2 in docs/components/neural/summarizer.md §5.
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
skinparam activity {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  BackgroundColor #2E7D32
  DiamondBackgroundColor #ECEFF1
  DiamondFontColor #263238
  DiamondBorderColor #90A4AE
}
title Summarizer::extractive — split ▸ filter ▸ embed ▸ centroid ▸ MMR ▸ re-order

start
:**split_sentences(text)**
break on . ! ? — unless the buffer ends in a
known abbreviation (Dr. Mr. e.g. i.e. etc. …),
in which case keep accumulating;

if (sentences empty?) then (yes)
  :return "";
  stop
else (no)
endif

if (|sentences| ≤ num_sentences?) then (yes)
  :**return the whole text**
  nothing to select;
  stop
else (no)
endif

:**length filter**
keep min_sentence_length ≤ |s| ≤ max_sentence_length
(20 … 500 characters by default);

if (none survive?) then (yes)
  :return the first num_sentences sentences
  (unfiltered fallback);
  stop
else (no)
endif

:**embedder.embed_batch(valid)**
→ v₁ … vₙ  (cached, ℓ₂-normalized);

:**centroid**  c = v̄ / ‖v̄‖;

:**relevance**  rel(sᵢ) = cos(vᵢ, c)
paired with each sentence's //original// index;

:**select_diverse** — greedy MMR
(see the MMR figure);

if (preserve_order?) then (true — default)
  :sort the picks by original index
  → the summary reads in document order;
else (false)
  :keep MMR selection order
  → most central sentence first;
endif

:join with " "  ⟶  **summary**;
stop

note right
  **Known defect — index misalignment.**
  select_diverse sorts its `scored` slice by relevance
  //in place//, but `embeddings` keeps document order.
  The redundancy term then reads embeddings[i] with i =
  position in the **sorted** slice, so it compares the
  wrong vectors (src/neural/summarizer.rs:202, :212).
  Relevance is carried inside the tuple and is therefore
  correct; selection still favours central, distinct
  sentences, but the diversity penalty is not the MMR
  quantity of the figure. Reported, not worked around.
end note

@enduml
